es  um the first appendix um sets out a more  qualitative  approach in terms of  how we've met our key business plan  priorities  and this mirror is the approach that we  took last financial year um in our  year-end annual report  um the second appendix is the more  qualitative um set of key performance  indicators which supplements that  so i think the content itself should be  reasonably self-explanatory  um and we have tried to um obviously  give explanations of um where  performance has varied against our key  performance indicators  so  unless anyone has any particular  comments or questions on on the content  of those then  the report is just noting thank you  thank you naomi any questions members  no thank you  okay members so there is one  recommendation set out at paragraph 1.1  to note the contents of this report and  appendices 1 and two  is this no tip members  thank you  okay we move on to agenda item  eight  advice services contract 2022-2024  who is the moss we'll present this  report thank you louisa thank you chair  members this is a report recommending  that  we enter into a procurement process for  the retender of the advisory services  contract it's a two-year contract with  the option for a one-year extension the  value of the contract is 70 000 per year  and that's been the same cost for the  last actually six years for the last two  lots of terms of this contract the  current provider of the advisory  services contract is citizens of ice  south essex and their contract comes  naturally to the end at  the beginning of next year which is why  we're proposing the procurement starts  at that time  in the reports you can see that there's  some evidence to show why an advisory  services contract is so integral to  enhancing our services and aligns itself  with the prevention agenda generally and  some last six months outputs from  citizens of ice give you a flavor and  headline of just how much support they  give to key services within our  organization  and hopefully the rest of the report is  relatively self-explanatory but if there  are any questions then please do  ask  thank you louisa members any questions  councillor smith  thank you um as as you've said um  we've had this contract uh this price  for quite some time with uh citizens  advised we are out of curiosity than  anything but are there any other  players in the market who can provide  this service  um there are which is why we continue to  go out to uh procurement  there are some services although they  some not completely comparable  but we do know neighbouring authorities  have gone for other providers so it's  only fair and open that we should  continue to put this through a proper  procurement process accordingly but as i  say we are sometimes comparing and pairs  with apples but  there are other providers that provide  similar services but not all the  services that our current provider  offers  thank you louisa any other questions  members  no okay thank you  sorry councillor webb  thank you chair it's just more of a  comment really um just to looking at the  numbers here that they're excellent in  terms of meeting the needs of our local  residents  i think one of the things i  really appreciated when i had this  portfolio was the value of these  services out to our residents and it's  fantastic that as a district we're still  able to provide this level of service  because we need our residents need this  support and help at times so i'd like to  recommend this service to you thank you  thank you councillor webb  so members there are two recommendations  set out at paragraph 1.1  1.1 to agree that the advice services  contract should be retended  for a further two-year period with the  option for the council to extend the  contract for a further one-year period  it is proposed that the value of the  contract would continue to be seventy  thousand pounds per year  one point two to recommend that this  report is presented to full council on 