ring  forward report to consider using the  council's compulsory purchase  powers to acquire land at the michelin  farm rally  once initial investigations and survey  works have been undertaken  1.2  to approve a drawdown from reserves of  up to twenty five thousand pounds to  enable officers to prepare a business  case the compulsory purchase of land at  michelin farm rally  one point three to delegate  responsibility  responsibility  to the assistant director place and  environment and assistant director legal  and democratic  in consultation with the portfolio  holder for strategic planning  to negotiate the potential voluntary  purchase of the land  in parallel to the compulsory purchase  order  process  and report this back to the executive  for consideration  members i will move those from the chair  do i have a second to please  counsel fd  members are you happy to vote vote for  the three recommendations on block  thank you can those members in favor  please raise their hands  thank you members that's carried  okay moving on to item 10  council program management office  and angela hutchins will  present this report thank you angela  thank you chairman um in relation to  this report members you'll recognize  this as being the quarterly report of  the council's program management office  in relation to the key programs which  the council is  undertaking  the report itself is self-explanatory  but we are available for questions  should you have any  members should note that if the  partnership with brentwood borough  council is approved in the new year the  transformation programme required to  implement the ambitions of that  partnership will effectively become the  program management office and  effectively subsume this report going  forward so this is  at this stage potentially the last  report in this format thank you  thank you very much members any  questions  no okay thank you  remember the members there is one  recommendation set out in paragraph 1.1  